# ClauseDesk

Contract clause extraction with verified citations.
NOT a chatbot. NOT legal advice.

## Core principle
**LLM reads. Code verifies. Human decides.**

## Current implementation state
Backend skeleton only. The LLM layer does not exist yet — rules in
`30-llm.mdc` describe the target architecture for when it is added.

## v1 scope
Upload contract → extract 8 clause types → verify quotes → review queue →
export report.

## 8 clause types (only these in v1)
`termination`, `liability_cap`, `governing_law`, `payment_terms`,
`confidentiality`, `ip_ownership`, `renewal`, `non_compete`

## Out of scope — never build (whole project)
- Legal advice or interpretation of clauses
- Chat interface
- Mobile app
- Payment processing
- Contract drafting or editing
- German law contracts (US commercial contracts only)
- More than 8 clause types

## Out of scope — deferred (not in v1)
- RAG (retrieval-augmented generation), embeddings, or vector stores
- Multi-step agents, tool-calling, planner/executor loops
- Async job queues (Celery, Redis, FastAPI BackgroundTasks)
- Provider fallback logic (single provider per call)
- Auto-approve of high-confidence clauses (human review always required)

## Data scope
- Primary evaluation set: CUAD (public, CC BY 4.0, English US
  commercial contracts)
- User uploads: stored 30 days, then deleted
- No contract text sent to LLM for training